@startuml logic-layers

' Logic layers for organizing measure logic, summarizing the Logic Layers topic.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #44546A
skinparam ArrowFontColor #44546A
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #44546A
  BorderThickness 1
  FontColor #1F2933
  roundCorner 10
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDF5
  BorderColor #B7A87A
  FontColor #4A4231
  FontSize 11
}

rectangle "== Measure\n//Who is in which population?//\n\n**Contains** population criteria,\nstratifiers, supplemental data\n\n**Must not contain** anything else" as measure #EEF2F7
rectangle "== Inferences\n//What do the records mean?//\n\n**Contains** clinical classification,\ncorrelation, temporal scoping\n\n**Must not contain** population criteria" as inferences #F7F9FB
rectangle "== Elements\n//Which records count?//\n\n**Contains** retrieves, status,\nintent and validity filters\n\n**Must not contain** thresholds,\nencounters, populations" as elements #F7F9FB
rectangle "== Concepts\n//What do we mean?//\n\n**Contains** valueset, code, codesystem,\naccessor functions\n\n**Must not contain** any expression" as concepts #EEF2F7

measure -down-> inferences : references
inferences -down-> elements : references
elements -down-> concepts : references

note right of measure
  The measure's contract.
  Readable at a glance, so a
  clinical reviewer can check
  the measure's //shape// without
  reading any computation.
end note

note right of elements
  **Configuration libraries** hold
  thresholds, ingredient strengths
  and similar inputs that are not
  in the patient record.
end note

note right of concepts
  A **Common** library is concepts
  plus accessors, and no retrieves:
  FHIRCommon, USCoreCommon,
  USQualityCoreCommon.
end note

note as direction #F2F7F2
  **References always point down.**
  A lower layer never references a higher one,
  which is what keeps each layer reviewable
  on its own.
end note

concepts -[hidden]down- direction

@enduml
